      "@id": "https://github.com/ferinazumaDEV/prompt-engineering-evidence#work",
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "name": "Evidence-Based Prompt Engineering",
      "headline": "A prompt-engineering reference where every technique is graded and sourced",
      "description": "A prompt-engineering reference in which every technique is graded solid, mixed or folklore, and every claim names a primary source. The evidence lives in a machine-readable ledger. This first release grades eight techniques (three solid, two mixed, three folklore) and ships one offline reproducible experiment; it is a sourced starting corpus, not an exhaustive survey. Effects that can only be measured with live model calls are recorded as dated snapshots against a named model, never as standing truths.",
      "abstract": "A prompt-engineering reference in which every technique is graded solid, mixed or folklore, and every claim names a primary source. The evidence lives in a machine-readable ledger. This first release grades eight techniques (three solid, two mixed, three folklore) and ships one offline reproducible experiment; it is a sourced starting corpus, not an exhaustive survey. Effects that can only be measured with live model calls are recorded as dated snapshots against a named model, never as standing truths.",
